 the county&rsquo;s 6 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 35 of them. In 2025 that same pair came in at 50% of normal on the middle of the grids, and January to February came in at 56%. So far in 2026, the middle of the grids came in at 67% of normal in April to May and 89% in June to July. Every grid had its driest year in 1965, and grid 24223 bottomed out at 62% of normal that year.</p>"}
